{"step_index":185,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T02:36:24Z","input_tokens":7664,"cache_read_tokens":35317,"output_tokens":3054,"thinking":"Four subagents are running concurrently for Batch 1. Consideration arises: Should Batch 2 commence immediately, or is there a need to await Batch 1's completion?\n\n\nAwaiting Batch 1's completion is prudent to prevent API rate limit issues observed previously. Limiting concurrency to four subagents per batch ensures stream reliability, while allowing inspection of the output and updating of the task list before proceeding. The system's asynchronous nature allows for other non-conflicting preparation tasks during this wait.\n\n\nAn automated script can be created to verify article quality upon batch completion. This script will validate file link existence and line number ranges within those files, ensuring that the necessary content sections are present and that Mermaid diagrams adhere to supported types, avoiding incorrect constructs. It will also check for unescaped dollar signs outside of valid code environments.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Automated quality gate verifier for /home/ethen/workspace/github/ethenslab/work/art-wiki/*.md.\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nWIKI_DIR = Path(\"/home/ethen/workspace/github/ethenslab/work/art-wiki\")\n\nSUPPORTED_MERMAID = (\n    \"flowchart \",\n    \"graph \",\n    \"sequenceDiagram\",\n    \"stateDiagram-v2\",\n    \"stateDiagram\",\n    \"classDiagram\",\n    \"erDiagram\",\n    \"xychart-beta\",\n)\n\nFILE_LINK_RE = re.compile(r\"\\]\\((file:///[^)#\\s]+)(?:#L(\\d+)(?:-L?(\\d+))?)?\\)\")\nUNQUOTED_NODE_SPECIAL_RE = re.compile(r'\\b[A-Za-z0-9_]+\\[(?!\")[^\\]\\n]*[()<>:/][^\\]\\n]*\\]')\nALERT_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\s*>\\s*\\[!(NOTE|TIP|IMPORTANT|WARNING|CAUTION)\\]\")\n\n\ndef check_file(md_path: Path) -> list[str]:\n    errors: list[str] = []\n    text = md_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    lines = text.splitlines()\n\n    if len(lines) < 250 and md_path.name != \"README.md\":\n        errors.append(f\"Too short ({len(lines)} lines < 250 expected)\")\n\n    # 1. Check required sections for mechanism wikis\n    if md_path.name != \"README.md\":\n        for kw in (\"What\", \"Why\", \"How\", \"能利用这个机制做什么\"):\n            if kw not in text:\n                errors.append(f\"Missing required section keyword: {kw}\")\n        if \"```mermaid\" not in text:\n            errors.append(\"Missing Mermaid diagram\")\n        if \"```text\" not in text and \"┌\" not in text and \"+---\" not in text:\n            errors.append(\"Missing ASCII/Unicode structure diagram\")\n\n    # 2. Check file:// links and line ranges\n    file_links = FILE_LINK_RE.findall(text)\n    if len(file_links) < 5:\n        errors.append(f\"Too few file:// source links ({len(file_links)})\")\n    line_count_cache: dict[str, int] = {}\n    for uri, l_start, l_end in file_links:\n        fs_path = uri[len(\"file://\") :]\n        if not os.path.exists(fs_path):\n            errors.append(f\"Broken file link: {uri}\")\n            continue\n        if os.path.isfile(fs_path) and l_start:\n            if fs_path not in line_count_cache:\n                with open(fs_path, \"rb\") as f:\n                    line_count_cache[fs_path] = sum(1 for _ in f)\n            max_line = line_count_cache[fs_path]\n            s = int(l_start)\n            e = int(l_end) if l_end else s\n            if s < 1 or e > max_line + 5 or s > e:\n                errors.append(\n                    f\"Out-of-range line link {uri}#L{l_start}\"\n                    + (f\"-L{l_end}\" if l_end else \"\")\n                    + f\" (file has {max_line} lines)\"\n                )\n\n    # 3. Check Mermaid blocks & consecutive GitHub Alerts\n    in_code = False\n    in_mermaid = False\n    mermaid_first_line_checked = False\n    mermaid_type = \"\"\n    prev_was_alert_block = False\n    in_alert_block = False\n\n    for idx, line in enumerate(lines, start=1):\n        stripped = line.strip()\n        if stripped.startswith(\"```\") or stripped.startswith(\"~~~~\"):\n            fence = stripped[:3]\n            if not in_code:\n                in_code = True\n                if stripped.startswith(\"```mermaid\"):\n                    in_mermaid = True\n                    mermaid_first_line_checked = False\n                    mermaid_type = \"\"\n            else:\n                in_code = False\n                in_mermaid = False\n            in_alert_block = False\n            continue\n\n        if in_mermaid:\n            if not stripped or stripped.startswith(\"%%\"):\n                continue\n            if not mermaid_first_line_checked:\n                mermaid_first_line_checked = True\n                mermaid_type = stripped\n                if not any(stripped.startswith(t) for t in SUPPORTED_MERMAID):\n                    errors.append(f\"Line {idx}: Unsupported Mermaid diagram header '{stripped}'\")\n            elif mermaid_type.startswith((\"flowchart\", \"graph\")):\n                if UNQUOTED_NODE_SPECIAL_RE.search(stripped):\n                    errors.append(\n                        f\"Line {idx}: Unquoted special chars in flowchart node label: {stripped}\"\n                    )\n            continue\n\n        if in_code:\n            continue\n\n        # Alert check outside code blocks\n        if ALERT_RE.match(line):\n            if prev_was_alert_block or in_alert_block:\n                errors.append(f\"Line {idx}: Consecutive or nested GitHub Alert\")\n            in_alert_block = True\n        elif stripped.startswith(\">\"):\n            # Continuation of blockquote / alert\n            pass\n        elif stripped == \"\":\n            if in_alert_block:\n                prev_was_alert_block = True\n                in_alert_block = False\n        else:\n            prev_was_alert_block = False\n            in_alert_block = False\n\n    return errors\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    targets = sorted(WIKI_DIR.glob(\"*.md\"))\n    if not targets:\n        print(f\"No markdown files found in {WIKI_DIR}\")\n        return 1\n\n    total_errors = 0\n    for md in targets:\n        errs = check_file(md)\n        line_cnt = sum(1 for _ in md.open(\"rb\"))\n        if errs:\n            print(f\"[WARN] {md.name} ({line_cnt} lines): {len(errs)} issue(s)\")\n            for e in errs:\n                print(f\"   - {e}\")\n            total_errors += len(errs)\n        else:\n            print(f\"[PASS] {md.name} ({line_cnt} lines)\")\n\n    return 1 if total_errors else 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"/home/ethen/.gemini/antigravity/brain/db260ba4-b7ce-4b54-9228-5adc342f0f21/scratch/verify_art_wikis.py"}},{"name":"edit_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Mark Batch 1 (Tasks 01-04) as in progress in task checklist.","UserFacing":true},"Path":"/home/ethen/.gemini/antigravity/brain/db260ba4-b7ce-4b54-9228-5adc342f0f21/task.md","Replacement":"## 专题一：App 执行、编译与启动性能加速机制\n- [/] **Task 01**：研究并输出 `01-tiered-execution-and-jit-aot.md` —— 混合执行引擎与分层编译机制（Switch / Nterp / Fast Baseline JIT / Optimizing JIT & OSR / AOT）\n- [/] **Task 02**：研究并输出 `02-pgo-profile-and-dexopt-pipeline.md` —— PGO 热点画像采集与编译治理闭环（`ProfileSaver` / `profman` / Cloud DM / `artd` & Pre-reboot Dexopt）\n- [/] **Task 03**：研究并输出 `03-app-startup-and-image-caching.md` —— App 启动加速与类/镜像预热机制（BootImage / JitZygote / AppImage / `RuntimeImage` / `StartupCompletedTask` / `madvise`）\n- [/] **Task 04**：研究并输出 `04-fast-jni-transition-optimization.md` —— 高性能 JNI 跨界调用优化机制（Normal JNI / `@FastNative` / `@CriticalNative` 与编译器 JNI Stub）","Target":"## 专题一：App 执行、编译与启动性能加速机制\n- [ ] **Task 01**：研究并输出 `01-tiered-execution-and-jit-aot.md` —— 混合执行引擎与分层编译机制（Switch / Nterp / Fast Baseline JIT / Optimizing JIT & OSR / AOT）\n- [ ] **Task 02**：研究